      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Find the real solution to the equation ${x}^{7}=-\\frac{1}{128}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We can solve this equation by taking the $7$th root of each side and solving for $x.$ Since $n=7$ is odd, there is only one real solution to this equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{7} & =-\\frac{1}{128} \\\\ \\sqrt[7]{{x}^{7}} & =\\sqrt[7]{(-\\frac{1}{128})} \\\\ x & =\\sqrt[7]{{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{7}} \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$",
